message.content:
Below is a minimal example of a “rotating card” that spins around its Y‑axis when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy the code into an `.html` file and open it in a browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<style>
/* Container that gives perspective to the card */
.card-wrapper {
  width: 300px;
  height: 200px;
  margin: 50px auto;
  perspective: 800px;          /* Creates a 3‑D space */
}

/* The card itself */
.card {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ff9a9e 0%, #fad0c4 100%);
  border-radius: 12px;
  box-shadow: 0 10px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
  transition: transform 0.6s ease;   /* Smooth rotation */
  transform-style: preserve-3d;      /* Keep children in 3‑D space */
  position: relative;
}

/* Hover effect – rotate 180° around Y axis */
.card:hover {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
}

/* Front & back faces */
.card .face {
  position: absolute;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  backface-visibility: hidden;   /* Hide back face when rotated */
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  font-size: 1.5rem;
  color: #fff;
  border-radius: 12px;
}

.card .front {
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ff9a9e 0%, #fad0c4 100%);
}

.card .back {
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, #a18cd1 0%, #fbc2eb 100%);
  transform: rotateY(180deg);     /* Position back face opposite */
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <div class="face front">Front Side</div>
    <div class="face back">Back Side</div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Element | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `.card-wrapper` | Provides a 3‑D perspective so the rotation looks realistic. |
| `.card` | The element that actually rotates. `transform-style: preserve-3d` keeps its children in 3‑D space. |
| `.face` | Both front and back faces share common styling. |
| `.back` | Rotated 180° so it appears on the other side of the card. |
| `backface-visibility: hidden` | Hides the back face when it’s turned away from the viewer. |

You can replace the gradients, colors, or text with your own content.  
Happy coding!
